INFO 10308 :: Page 166 :: 11.30 PM Tunnel Hill May 8 1864 Tunnel Hill Station Georgia Eight For Gen Halleck Wash 6 PM ---- dispatch of today is received ---- am delighted at the arrangement & it shall receive my most hearty concurrence ---- I will teleg very full to Genl Canby by today at Cairo ---- I have been all day reconnoitering the mountain through whose gorge the RR & common road passes ---- By tonight McPherson will be in Snake Creek Gap threatening Ruasca & tomorrow all will move to the attack ---- Army in good spirits & condition ---- I hope Johnston will fight here instead of drawing me far down into Georgia sig Gen Sherman 4 am 4.15 AM 9th Maj Eckert ---- Jamestown Va May 9/64 I left Gen Butler Head Quarters five miles from White River Landing 9 PM all quiet and ready to move in morning ---- Wests Cavalry Expedition crossing at Harrisons Landing to join us I will start line tomorrow all working fine will endeavor to keep you posted R OBrien
INFO 10291 :: Page 149 :: society, men whose intended raising has been postponed but the preparation for which rebel cavalry from the south were already beginning would seize that opportunity burn our depot & do us irreparable damage ---- This matter of the secret society must be kept perfectly secret until I can secure names and residence which will enable me to seize and convict the ring leaders and crush the organization which is wide spread ---- If you think it safe after my statements of, these, facts, to, risk sending off, these troops, with out bringing some disciplined Infantry to take their place your orders will be obeyed sig Rosecrans Mart Crain is here in military office working nights have some hopes of him reforming and making a steady man I hope he will 1115 PM JW Sampson Balto - Ft Monroe May 1" 1864 For Gen Liu Wallace Correspondant of the N. Y. World at Baltimore & also from Ft Monroe is WW Shore whom I sent away from this Dept ---- Please arrest him and send him to me ---- I have found in the Richmond papers that his articles are giving aid and comfort to the Enemy sig BF Butler
